MLX 0.32.3 inserted a `const std::optional<array>& global_scale` parameter
into gather_qmm before `sorted_indices`. mlx-c v0.7.0 (written for MLX 0.32.2)
passes `sorted_indices` (bool) in its place, which fails to compile against
0.32.3. mlx-c v0.8.0 adds the parameter but also binds mlx::core::unique,
which only exists from MLX 0.32.4, so it does not build against 0.32.3.
Shim: pass no global scale; ming-tts does not use it. Drop this patch when moving to MLX >= 0.32.4 + mlx-c v0.8.0.

--- a/mlx/c/ops.cpp
+++ b/mlx/c/ops.cpp
@@ -1708,6 +1708,8 @@ extern "C" int mlx_gather_qmm(
             (bits.has_value ? std::make_optional<int>(bits.value)
                             : std::nullopt),
             std::string(mode),
+            /* global_scale: no C ABI surface yet */
+            std::nullopt,
             sorted_indices,
             mlx_stream_get_(s)));
   } catch (std::exception& e) {
